{
  "description": "Media controls vectors (changelog 57). Spec: docs/protocol.md, \"Media controls: media.*\". Both apps run every array except where a row says one platform. The media.* frames themselves are in messages.json (the media-* cases).",
  "specVersion": 1,
  "howToRead": "limits: every limit of the spec in one place. limiters: the five rate limits of 3.6 (a token bucket: capacity and tokens per second; or a sliding window: at most max in windowMs); errorSpacingMs = at most one error answer in that time. sid[]: identity (an Android package name or a Windows SourceAppUserModelId) -> sid (first 32 hex of SHA-256 of its UTF-8 bytes). clean[]: field + input -> expected after the five steps of link.title (null = absent); the limit is limits[field]. inputParts and expectedParts write a long text as a list of parts: a string is taken as it is, [text, n] is text repeated n times. image[]: a media.image frame is built from kind, hash and the file dataFile (a path relative to protocol/, base64url of its bytes) and expect says accepted, dropped (silently, counted) or bad_request; hash is the hash of the file unless hash is given; the wire check reads the magic and the size from the headers and decodes nothing (the apps' own decoders drop a picture they can't decode). position[]: what the viewer shows elapsedMs after a media.state arrived: expect.positionMs (null if the state had no position) and expect.state (a playing state whose extrapolated position is more than 5 s past durationMs is shown paused at the end; rateMilli 0 is shown paused); rateMilli absent means 1000. sourcePosition[]: the source's own position for now: platform android (positionMs is -1 if unknown; speed is the PlaybackState number; updateTimeMs and nowMs are on one monotonic clock) or windows (positionTicks, lastUpdatedTicks and nowTicks are decimal strings of 100 ns ticks; rateMilli null = 1000; lastUpdatedTicks 0 = never updated); null if unknown; clamped to 0..durationMs when there is one. pick[]: sessions in the platform's priority order (own = Kin's own session, title = has a title, pausedMs = how long it has been paused) and current (the sid shown now, or null) -> expect (a sid, or null for none). clearDebounce[]: events in time order (present = some candidate exists after the event) -> the times a media.clear goes out (a session is shown when the run starts; a clear goes out 1500 ms after the first event with nothing present if nothing is present again; a case ends with an event at or after the due time). throttle[]: events (t, value) -> what goes on the wire (the first goes at once if the last send was 250 ms ago or more, else the latest value is held and goes at last + 250; a value equal to the last sent one is not sent; the end of the events flushes what is held). rate[]: limiter + events as [t, count] pairs (count events at time t) -> expect as [outcome, count] runs, and errorsAt = the times an error answer goes out. androidMap[]: a PlaybackState (state int, actions bit mask, speed number) and hasDuration -> candidate, state, actions (canonical order play, pause, toggle, next, prev, seek), rateMilli. toAndroid[]: wire state and actions -> PlaybackState state int and actions mask (viewer on Android). windowsMap[]: a GSMTC status (Closed 0, Opened 1, Changing 2, Stopped 3, Playing 4, Paused 5), the Controls flags (position = IsPlaybackPositionEnabled) and durationMs (0 = unknown) -> candidate, state, actions. toSmtc[]: wire state and actions and testMode -> the SystemMediaTransportControls status and which buttons are enabled (testMode never shows Playing). volumeLevel[]: native volume -> level (windows: scalar 0..1; android: index and max). volumeSet[]: a media.cmd volume op on a native volume -> the result (windows: steps = the endpoint's step count, level = the current level; android: max and index; the result is a level, an index or muted). sendRule[]: may a source send media.state/image/volume/clear (kind), or a viewer a media.cmd (cmd), or either a media.status (status): hellos = the capability lists of the peer's accepted hellos in order, status = the peer's latest media.status or null, ownShare, shareJustTurnedOff (the one media.clear a source sends when its share goes off) -> send or nothing. viewerRule[]: a viewer whose show is off drops media.state/image/clear/volume silently (counted), whatever the sender did. cmdResult[]: what a source answers to a media.cmd, in the order disabled, rate_limited, not_found, stale, action_failed, else ok (no reply). All non-ASCII characters are written as escapes.",
  "limits": {"app":40,"title":150,"artist":100,"album":100,"actions":8,"durationMs":86400000,"positionMs":86400000,"rateMilli":4000,"seekMs":86400000,"level":100,"delta":100,"stateFrameSend":16384,"stateFrameRecv":32768,"imageFrame":49152,"imageBytes":24576,"artPixels":256,"iconPixels":128,"imageMinPixels":16,"pausedExpiryMs":1800000,"clearDebounceMs":1500,"positionJumpMs":1500,"endGraceMs":5000,"throttleMs":250},
